  "findings": [
    "SequenceDiagram#getLastEventWithNote scans events for EventWithNote, including AbstractMessage/MessageExo. FactorySequenceNoteOnArrowCommand attaches the Note; Step1MessageExo#createArrow builds NoteBox objects and wraps the arrow in ArrowAndNoteBox. Updating last_message from normalized from/to endpoints correctly preserves this narrow ownership data flow; no fallback participant or coordinate correction was added.",
    "Fresh positive cases retain20 Note events after versus16 before. Every fresh note label has exactly the same multiplicity in Java and final Rust. Incoming/outgoing left/right normalized endpoints, consecutive external messages, ordinary-after-external replacement, nested groups, and explicit over-note controls are recorded in note-ownership.json. Multiline notes could already exist before with empty participants and on_message=false; the packet corrects ownership even when event count does not change.",
    "Fresh18 includes16 Java-valid inputs and two Java-invalid bare-over controls. Positive whole matches improve2 to9; seven SVG mismatches remain. Outgoing left/right multiline notes fail both engines, incoming-right and prior-ordinary incoming-right fail legacy, and nested external group fails legacy. The preserved all2371 replay also keeps the named imported and maker external-note envelope failures. Thus the maker claim that horizontal envelopes remain unrepaired is confirmed.",
    "The two bare note-over forms are rejected by Java but accepted before and after by Rust, and earn no positive parity credit. No new valid-input error or renderer panic occurs. Whole failures reject the mechanism despite retained note labels and correct normalized owner fields."
  ],
